Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:02:37 +0800
Subject: core/session: say why the provider's safety filter stopped a response

A refusal showed only "Provider blocked the response". Anthropic sends the reason with it:
stop_details { type: "refusal", category, explanation } on the message_delta (category and
explanation may be null). The Anthropic parser now keeps stop_details on the finish's provider
metadata, and the error reads e.g.

  The provider's safety filter stopped the response (category: cyber): This request was
  declined because it could enable cyber harm. Retrying the same conversation is usually
  stopped again: edit or rephrase your last message, or switch model.

or "It gave no reason." when there are no details (OpenAI, Gemini). Compaction summaries get
the same message.

Ocelot-Patch: core/refusal-reason

